// Impervious Sphere

@0 = ~Metal Orb~
@1 = ~Impervious Sphere~

@10 = ~This construct is spherical in shape and consists of a pulsating light source that is held in place by a copper frame. Runes covering the frame indicate that magic was involved in the creation of the orb.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 2~
@11 = ~A gnomish maxim states: “Nothing can hurt you if nothing can reach you. Nothing can help you either.”

Among the more peculiar inventions of gnomish defensive engineering, the Impervious Sphere was devised by artificers who believed that the ultimate form of protection was not armor, but complete separation from danger. When activated, the device unfolds a shimmering spherical barrier around the bearer, sealing them away from the world for several turns.

While within the sphere, the bearer cannot interact with the outside world. Neither sword nor spell can harm the occupant. However, they can see or be seen vaguely through its curiously pink opacity. Unfortunately, the protection is absolute: the bearer can neither strike nor receive aid from the outside. The sphere carries only a limited reserve of breathable air, making prolonged use a matter of careful timing rather than simple safety.

Gnomish sages insist that the device was inspired by a particularly disastrous experiment involving a runaway alchemical engine. Its inventor, Fizzwick Brassbubble, reportedly survived the resulting explosion perfectly unharmed—only to discover that he had sealed himself inside the sphere for several minutes while standing directly atop the laboratory's emergency release lever. As a result, the device was subsequently adjusted so that the user could move around—albeit very slowly.

STATISTICS:

Charge abilities:
– Impervious Sphere
  Duration: 1d4 turns
  Area of Effect: The user
  Surrounds the user by a protective barrier that makes them completely immune to all physical and magical damage, but also prevents any interaction with the outside world. The user is able to walk at 20% of normal walking speed and may run out of breathable air after 1d4-1 turns, which causes 1d4 non-lethal damage per round until the barrier wears off.

Weight: 2~

@20 = ~Impervious Sphere~
@21 = ~Suffocation~
